WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.520
- My next guests have released
one of the hottest albums

00:00:02.520 --> 00:00:03.353
of the summer.

00:00:03.353 --> 00:00:05.530
They're a really, truly talented duo.

00:00:05.530 --> 00:00:08.720
It's called "Ungodly Hour"
and it's getting rave reviews.

00:00:08.720 --> 00:00:10.960
They're signed to their
mentor, Beyonce's, label.

00:00:10.960 --> 00:00:12.020
Not too shabby.

00:00:12.020 --> 00:00:14.181
Give it up for sisters Chloe and Halle.

00:00:14.181 --> 00:00:15.061
- Hi!

00:00:15.061 --> 00:00:16.110
- How are you?

00:00:16.110 --> 00:00:17.350
- I am so good.

00:00:17.350 --> 00:00:19.270
I know we've never officially met

00:00:19.270 --> 00:00:21.622
but we have been on a song together.

00:00:21.622 --> 00:00:22.455
- Yeah (laughs).

00:00:22.455 --> 00:00:23.600
- "This Is For My Girls"

00:00:23.600 --> 00:00:25.140
which was organized by Michelle Obama

00:00:25.140 --> 00:00:26.510
to raise money for girls' education.

00:00:26.510 --> 00:00:27.670
It was such a cool thing and

00:00:27.670 --> 00:00:29.770
honestly that's the first
time I'd heard of y'all

00:00:29.770 --> 00:00:32.460
and I was like, who are these
chicks singing right here?

00:00:32.460 --> 00:00:34.060
And you're so young!

00:00:34.060 --> 00:00:35.501
You're so talented.

00:00:35.501 --> 00:00:37.040
- Thank you.
- Thank you so much.

00:00:37.040 --> 00:00:38.890
We're such huge fans of you

00:00:38.890 --> 00:00:39.723
so thanks
- Oh!

00:00:39.723 --> 00:00:41.180
- for having me on today.

00:00:41.180 --> 00:00:42.210
- Well that is awesome.

00:00:42.210 --> 00:00:44.040
No, I went down the rabbit hole

00:00:44.040 --> 00:00:45.450
of YouTube videos with y'all last night.

00:00:45.450 --> 00:00:47.090
I love your songs, love your music.

00:00:47.090 --> 00:00:48.290
I love that it's like, bringing back

00:00:48.290 --> 00:00:49.560
what real R&amp;B sounds like

00:00:49.560 --> 00:00:51.349
from whenever I was in junior high.

00:00:51.349 --> 00:00:54.950
That's one of my favorite
parts of your sound.

00:00:54.950 --> 00:00:56.280
Is it kind of cool though,
speaking to Michelle Obama.

00:00:56.280 --> 00:00:58.310
You know we all got to do that together

00:00:58.310 --> 00:01:00.949
but she's been a big supporter of y'alls.

00:01:00.949 --> 00:01:01.860
- She really has.
- Yeah.

00:01:01.860 --> 00:01:04.610
- And every time, we pinch ourselves

00:01:04.610 --> 00:01:07.960
because, as you know,
she is as much of goddess

00:01:07.960 --> 00:01:10.710
as the world thinks she is so

00:01:10.710 --> 00:01:12.360
I love Mrs Obama.

00:01:12.360 --> 00:01:14.410
- That's just cool though,
that she's seeing you.

00:01:14.410 --> 00:01:15.930
That must feel really cool,

00:01:15.930 --> 00:01:18.620
to be seen by someone
like that is awesome.

00:01:18.620 --> 00:01:20.630
But speaking of powerful women,

00:01:20.630 --> 00:01:23.080
you're also signed to Beyonce's label.

00:01:23.080 --> 00:01:24.870
My fellow Texas girl, I love her.

00:01:24.870 --> 00:01:25.703
So I understand,

00:01:25.703 --> 00:01:28.480
she had no notes when
she heard your new album.

00:01:28.480 --> 00:01:29.313
Did that surprise you?

00:01:29.313 --> 00:01:30.950
Because I feel like she's kind of

00:01:30.950 --> 00:01:33.620
like me or all Texas women,
like, let's do it right

00:01:33.620 --> 00:01:36.100
let's get it done right and
she might be particular.

00:01:36.100 --> 00:01:37.410
- Yes, absolutely.

00:01:37.410 --> 00:01:39.290
I mean, on our prior projects

00:01:39.290 --> 00:01:42.300
there would definitely be more notes

00:01:42.300 --> 00:01:45.170
because she's an amazing perfectionist

00:01:45.170 --> 00:01:48.160
and we love that and admire
that about her you know.

00:01:48.160 --> 00:01:50.430
She's always been one of
our biggest inspirations

00:01:50.430 --> 00:01:52.870
so when we presented this album to her

00:01:52.870 --> 00:01:56.210
it was very little and minor things

00:01:56.210 --> 00:01:58.750
and we were like, wow,
she must really like it.

00:01:58.750 --> 00:02:01.140
So we were very, very happy about that.

00:02:01.140 --> 00:02:05.100
- Well you both, you pushed
the release of your new album

00:02:05.100 --> 00:02:06.580
to honor George Floyd.

00:02:06.580 --> 00:02:08.800
How are you interpreting
this moment in our country?

00:02:08.800 --> 00:02:10.510
'Cause you're of the younger generation

00:02:10.510 --> 00:02:13.100
and you're very powerful
and I think we've all been

00:02:13.100 --> 00:02:15.430
really impressed with how
the younger generation

00:02:15.430 --> 00:02:16.810
is handling all of this.

00:02:16.810 --> 00:02:19.320
How have you specifically
been handling it?

00:02:19.320 --> 00:02:20.210
- Thank you, yes.

00:02:20.210 --> 00:02:22.730
Well, the first couple of weeks

00:02:22.730 --> 00:02:24.870
when everything was
happening we were definitely

00:02:24.870 --> 00:02:28.750
just very sad and I feel like collectively

00:02:28.750 --> 00:02:31.640
in our community of our
black brothers and sisters

00:02:31.640 --> 00:02:34.420
it's like this collective
feeling of trauma

00:02:34.420 --> 00:02:36.570
when something like that happens because

00:02:36.570 --> 00:02:39.220
for me personally, I think
of my little brother,

00:02:39.220 --> 00:02:40.513
we think of our dad.

00:02:41.430 --> 00:02:42.960
That could have been them.

00:02:42.960 --> 00:02:46.240
So we just are trying to
do everything that we can

00:02:46.240 --> 00:02:49.590
to continue to lift each
other up with our voices

00:02:49.590 --> 00:02:51.880
and demand justice for what's right.

00:02:51.880 --> 00:02:54.060
I mean, our color of our skin

00:02:54.060 --> 00:02:55.430
should not be a death sentence.

00:02:55.430 --> 00:02:58.780
People deserve to live a
beautiful and long life

00:02:58.780 --> 00:03:00.890
just like everyone else, so.
- Exactly, yeah.

00:03:00.890 --> 00:03:02.992
- I mean, it's crazy that's not a given.

00:03:02.992 --> 00:03:05.035
It's insane to me.

00:03:05.035 --> 00:03:08.040
Well Halle, you're set to play Ariel

00:03:08.040 --> 00:03:09.670
in the live action "Little Mermaid"

00:03:09.670 --> 00:03:11.160
which I'm super stoked about.

00:03:11.160 --> 00:03:12.850
That was one of my
favorites from childhood.

00:03:12.850 --> 00:03:16.520
So, what are you excited for
fans to see when it comes out?

00:03:16.520 --> 00:03:20.270
- Oh I'm just excited for
everyone to see the kind of

00:03:20.270 --> 00:03:24.690
upgraded but also still very close to home

00:03:24.690 --> 00:03:26.280
as the original I mean.

00:03:26.280 --> 00:03:29.390
The original was my favorite
when I was little as well.

00:03:29.390 --> 00:03:32.700
I think everybody really
connects with Ariel in a way

00:03:32.700 --> 00:03:37.170
and resonates with the feeling
of wanting to be somewhere

00:03:37.170 --> 00:03:40.400
and feel like home is another place

00:03:40.400 --> 00:03:42.410
so we are really excited for it

00:03:42.410 --> 00:03:44.760
and I just feel very
honored to take on that role

00:03:44.760 --> 00:03:48.160
to show other black girls that
they can be princesses too.

00:03:48.160 --> 00:03:49.360
- Yeah, representation.

00:03:49.360 --> 00:03:50.420
Agreed, agreed.

00:03:50.420 --> 00:03:52.610
I wanna compliment you on something too.

00:03:52.610 --> 00:03:53.590
Like watching you,

00:03:53.590 --> 00:03:56.760
you both have such
different energies and vibes

00:03:56.760 --> 00:04:00.420
and they both collide in
such a cool way that is so

00:04:01.360 --> 00:04:03.864
meaningful and I think it has to happen

00:04:03.864 --> 00:04:06.760
in order for a duo to actually work

00:04:06.760 --> 00:04:09.980
and it's very inspiring
to watch both of you.

00:04:09.980 --> 00:04:13.320
You're both so captivating
in completely different ways

00:04:13.320 --> 00:04:15.480
vocally, aesthetically, how
you move with your body,

00:04:15.480 --> 00:04:17.270
like everything is so different

00:04:17.270 --> 00:04:19.510
and yet it's like one unit

00:04:19.510 --> 00:04:20.850
and really, it's impressive.

00:04:20.850 --> 00:04:22.620
- Thank you.
- Thank you so much.

00:04:22.620 --> 00:04:23.970
That is so much

00:04:23.970 --> 00:04:25.080
coming from you.
- Yeah.

00:04:25.080 --> 00:04:28.160
- Oh well, it's incredible
to watch you, it's awesome.

00:04:28.160 --> 00:04:29.820
Well, thank you so much
for joining us ladies

00:04:29.820 --> 00:04:31.637
and everyone be sure to
check out their album

00:04:31.637 --> 00:04:33.220
"Ungodly Hour" right now.

00:04:33.220 --> 00:04:34.620
You're gonna want to get it.

